-- ============================================================================
-- DR1: Well Design & Surveys joins the catalog, the FIRST Drilling &
-- Completions course (plan of record: petrolord-suite docs/scope/
-- NextGen-Drilling-Courses-PLAN.md).
--
-- Catalog row (module 'drilling' mapped from day one so the Expert bridge
-- trigger can issue Suite discount codes) plus the three capstones. NO
-- prerequisite: this course is the ROOT of the drilling path, and the plan
-- sets no hard gate inside the module, so DR2 through DR12 will recommend it
-- rather than require it.
--
-- THE ENGINE. engines/drilling was vendored ahead of this wave: 25 modules
-- and about 6980 lines, with 23 golden fixtures generated by an independent
-- oracle. This course uses ten of them: the survey table and its four
-- classical methods, the Applied Drilling Engineering chapter 8 worked
-- example, the arc and S-profile solvers, the build-and-hold compiler, the
-- TVD crossing search, the toolface sphere, the ISCWSA MWD Rev4 validation
-- well, the ISCWSA standard clearance set, and the WMM2025 model with its
-- publisher's own test values.
--
-- THREE FIXTURES CARRY THE ASSOCIATE TIER, ONE WELL CARRIES THE PROFESSIONAL
-- TIER, AND ONE STANDARD SET CARRIES THE EXPERT TIER. That is deliberate: a
-- number learned in one lesson still means the same thing in the next, and
-- the tiers are separated by what they ASK of the same geometry rather than
-- by swapping the geometry out.
--
-- THE SCOPE DECISION THAT SHAPES THIS COURSE. engines/drilling implements
-- the ISCWSA MWD magnetic error model. It does NOT implement the gyroscopic
-- models, multi-station analysis, in-field referencing, relief well ranging,
-- or probabilistic collision risk. Expert module m05 l04 teaches all four
-- with their mechanisms and their value stated, and grades none of them.
-- That is the RC5 treatment of results literacy applied again, for the same
-- reason: teaching a number and certifying a learner can produce it are
-- different acts. 20260830_dr1_welldesign_go_live.sql asserts it.
--
-- WHY THE ASSOCIATE TIER GRADES A METHOD'S ERROR AND NOT ONLY ITS ANSWER.
-- Field 2 is the tangential method's TVD less the PUBLISHED minimum-curvature
-- TVD of 1653.99 ft, not less the engine's own 1653.986686265376. The two
-- differ in the third decimal, and the field's tolerance of 0.005 is tighter
-- than that gap, so the reference has to be the published number. Grading the
-- ERROR rather than the depth turns a warning about an obsolete method into a
-- measurement in feet, which is what changes what people do.
--
-- WHY THE EXPERT TIER GRADES THE SAME CASE TWICE. Fields 3 and 4 are offset
-- well 10's minimum separation factor at k 3.5 and at k 5.0. The factor is
-- NEGATIVE, so its numerator is fixed and only the denominator moves: raising
-- the confidence factor moves the number from about -0.607 to about -0.425,
-- an exact two-fifths ratio, which reads as an improvement without either
-- well having moved. Grading both forces the comparison to be made.
--
-- Oracle values reproduced from the vendored engine in Node BEFORE this
-- migration was written (DR1-TRUTH.md, verified field by field by
-- verify_fields.mjs: 18 of 18 exact); welldesignLab.test.js pins all eighteen
-- through the course's own teaching lab, so a panel and the live grader
-- cannot drift apart. Pairwise tolerance-collision check across all eighteen:
-- 0 fatal, 0 notes.
--
-- STATUS deliberately left 'coming_soon'. The flip to 'available' is what
-- makes the course enrollable and it is held in
-- 20260830_dr1_welldesign_go_live.sql until a production upload carries the
-- /dashboard/apps/welldesign route.
-- ============================================================================

-- ------------------------------------------------ 1. the catalog row
insert into public.academy_apps (slug, name, module, path_order, status, prereq_slug)
values ('welldesign', 'Well Design & Surveys', 'drilling', 18, 'coming_soon', null)
on conflict (slug) do nothing;

-- ------------------------------------------------ 2. the capstones
insert into public.academy_capstones
    (app_slug, tier, cert_tier, dataset, title, prompt, fields)
values
(
  'welldesign', 'beginner', 'associate',
  'three fixtures: the Applied Drilling Engineering chapter 8 survey of 21 stations in feet, the feet and metric golden wells with their own vertical section azimuths of 75 and 200 degrees, and the first published build-and-hold design',
  'Read the survey, and measure what a weaker method costs',
  'Six survey calculations on three fixtures. (1) On the Applied Drilling Engineering chapter 8 survey, compute the full minimum-curvature survey table and report the true vertical depth at the deepest station. (2) On that same survey, compute the tangential method''s true vertical depth, summing over intervals the interval length times the cosine of the inclination at the LOWER station of each interval, and report that value MINUS the published minimum-curvature true vertical depth of 1653.99 ft. The published value is the reference, not the engine''s own answer. (3) On the FEET golden well, report the true vertical depth at total depth. (4) On that same well, report the vertical section at total depth, using the fixture''s own reference azimuth of 75 degrees rather than any default. (5) On the METRIC golden well, using its stated reference azimuth of 200 degrees, report the north displacement at total depth; it is negative. (6) Compile the first published build-and-hold design, kicking off vertical, building at the stated rate to the stated inclination and holding for the stated length on the stated azimuth, and report the true vertical depth at the last row of the compiled table.',
  jsonb_build_array(
    jsonb_build_object('key','ade_mincurve_tvd',          'label','ADE chapter 8 minimum-curvature TVD','unit','ft','expected',1653.986686265376,  'tol',0.002),
    jsonb_build_object('key','ade_tangential_tvd_error',  'label','Tangential TVD less published value','unit','ft','expected',-25.38120586938976, 'tol',0.005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','golden_ft_tvd',             'label','Feet well TVD at total depth',       'unit','ft','expected',3686.9804661202493, 'tol',0.005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','golden_ft_vertical_section','label','Feet well vertical section',         'unit','ft','expected',1255.8726308373678, 'tol',0.005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','golden_m_north',            'label','Metric well north displacement',     'unit','m', 'expected',-1320.505235386686, 'tol',0.005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','buildhold_end_tvd',         'label','Compiled build-and-hold end TVD',    'unit','ft','expected',1481.1257260785915, 'tol',0.005)
  )
),
(
  'welldesign', 'intermediate', 'professional',
  'the ISCWSA MWD Rev4 validation well: 268 stations to 8000 m measured depth, starting vertical and ending horizontal at 90 degrees on a 75 degree azimuth, with the fixture''s own header at 50000 nT, 72 degrees dip, minus 4 degrees declination and zero convergence',
  'Read one station''s uncertainty, and say what pays for it',
  'Six quantities from ONE station of the ISCWSA MWD Rev4 validation well: the DEEPEST station, index 267 of 268, at 8000 m measured depth. Run the standard MWD Rev4 parameter set with no corrections applied, using the fixture''s own header: total field 50000 nT, dip 72 degrees, declination minus 4 degrees, convergence zero, azimuths referenced to true north, standard gravity, and the vertical inclination limit the fixture states. Report: (1) the north-north entry of the TOTAL covariance, which is a variance in square metres and not a sigma; (2) the LATERAL one-sigma uncertainty in the borehole frame, which needs the rotation from north-east-vertical and is not the east sigma; (3) the HIGHSIDE one-sigma uncertainty in that same frame; (4) the semi-major axis of the HORIZONTAL ellipse, built from the north-east block''s eigen-decomposition, at the two-dimensional 95 percent confidence factor of 2.7955; (5) the azimuth of that ellipse''s major axis in degrees, which does not depend on the confidence factor because scaling an ellipse does not rotate it; and (6) the percentage of the total variance contributed by the single largest source, measured by TRACE, that source''s three variances summed and divided by the same sum over all sources, times a hundred.',
  jsonb_build_array(
    jsonb_build_object('key','well1_cov_nn',             'label','North-north covariance entry',   'unit','m2',     'expected',8547.77693579118,    'tol',0.005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','well1_sigma_lateral',      'label','Lateral one-sigma',              'unit','m',      'expected',95.65082424690361,   'tol',0.005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','well1_sigma_highside',     'label','Highside one-sigma',             'unit','m',      'expected',21.636241962526093,  'tol',0.005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','well1_ellipse95_semimajor','label','Horizontal ellipse semi-major',  'unit','m',      'expected',267.39198828526287,  'tol',0.005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','well1_ellipse_azimuth_deg','label','Ellipse major axis azimuth',     'unit','deg',    'expected',165.05207648844214,  'tol',0.005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','well1_amil_share_pct',     'label','Largest source share by trace',  'unit','percent','expected',58.294649231431436,  'tol',0.005)
  )
),
(
  'welldesign', 'advanced', 'expert',
  'the ISCWSA standard clearance set: one reference well of 100 stations to 2940 m and eleven offsets in a shared frame, at the published parameters; and the WMM2025 geomagnetic model against its publisher''s twelve test values',
  'Separate two wells, and check the frame they are in',
  'Six numbers from the ISCWSA standard clearance set and the geomagnetic model. Use the published clearance parameters throughout: pedal-curve method, confidence factor 3.5, surface position sigma 0.5 m, tool projection allowance 0.3 m, reference hole radius 0.4572 m, offset hole radius 0.3048 m, and the ISCWSA MWD Rev4 error model with each well''s own header from the fixture. Report: (1) the MINIMUM separation factor over the reference well''s stations against offset 01; (2) the same against offset 09, which is very nearly zero; (3) the same against offset 10, the only case with a kickoff, supplying the kickoff depth the fixture states so the shared uncertainty above it is removed; it is NEGATIVE. (4) Rerun case 3 with the confidence factor raised to 5.0 and nothing else changed, and report that minimum. Compute it by rerunning rather than by scaling field 3. (5) Evaluate the WMM2025 model at each of the publisher''s twelve test points and report the LARGEST absolute declination error in degrees, a maximum and not a mean. (6) Report the declination the model gives at 80 degrees north, 0 degrees east, at sea level, at the epoch 2025.0.',
  jsonb_build_array(
    jsonb_build_object('key','well01_min_sf',              'label','Minimum separation factor, offset 01','unit','-',  'expected',1.400242036710446,   'tol',0.0005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','well09_min_sf',              'label','Minimum separation factor, offset 09','unit','-',  'expected',0.009794688844024428,'tol',0.00005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','well10_min_sf',              'label','Minimum separation factor, offset 10','unit','-',  'expected',-0.6068571428571429, 'tol',0.0005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','well10_min_sf_at_k5',        'label','Offset 10 minimum at k of 5.0',       'unit','-',  'expected',-0.4248,             'tol',0.0005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','wmm_max_declination_error_deg','label','Worst declination error, 12 points','unit','deg','expected',0.00461482429820137, 'tol',0.000005),
    jsonb_build_object('key','wmm_declination_at_80n_0e',  'label','Declination at 80N 0E, epoch 2025.0', 'unit','deg','expected',1.2814821161348655,  'tol',0.00005)
  )
)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do nothing;

